  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Concierge",
    "overview": "The admin is a concierge who is always ready and never in the way. The host comes in to check today's arrivals, record a phone booking, or close a weekend. The interface answers quickly, in plain French, and then gets out of the way. Expression lives in the details: a deep forest sidebar, a terracotta mark, warm linen behind white cards. The layout itself stays predictable.\n\nThe surface is warm and tactile, never clinical. Backgrounds are linen and oat rather than grey. Borders are sand-coloured. Controls have soft 8–12px corners, a 1.5px field stroke and a gentle shadow you can almost feel. Density is moderate: one screen shows a working day's worth of information without crowding. Text sizes are compact (13.5px body) because hosts scan, not read.\n\nGuest-facing sites are a different world on purpose. Each one belongs to the host (see *Public templates* under Components). The admin palette never leaks into them, and template palettes never leak into the admin.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Forest-green structure, terracotta as the rare warm accent.",
      "Warm neutrals (linen, oat, sand), never cool grey for surfaces.",
      "One sans family (Plus Jakarta Sans) carrying hierarchy through weight and tight tracking.",
      "Soft corners, light lift, flat at rest.",
      "Status colours are semantic and fixed; they mean the same thing on every screen."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Terracotta Whisper Rule",
        "body": "Terracotta marks identity and \"you are here\" — the logo tile, the active nav bar. It is never a button fill or a large surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Palettes Rule",
        "body": "`--admin-*` tokens live under `[data-admin]` and are used only in `/admin` and auth screens. The guest sites use the `--s-*` contract scoped under `.site[data-tpl]`. Never mix them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bounded Host Colour Rule",
        "body": "A host colour never reaches the page raw. It passes through `oklch(from … min(l, X) c h)` (or `max` for the Affiche sky) before any text sits on it. A new world sets its bound before it uses the colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Contract Rule",
        "body": "Shared structure (`components/public/site.css`) reads only `--s-*` tokens and holds no colour or font. A world's private variables (`--s-plate*`, `--l-*`, `--a-*`, `--st-*`) stay in its own file.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight-Not-Size Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from weight and tracking at compact sizes. Nothing in the admin goes above 28px.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lettering Rule",
        "body": "Where a world letters its objects (Plaque, Linge, Affiche), room numbers, prices, nav and buttons take the display face; the reading face is for sentences.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper-on-Linen Rule",
        "body": "Depth comes from white paper against warm linen plus a sand border first, and from shadow second. Never stack shadows to create hierarchy.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Invented Content Rule",
        "body": "A public block renders only from host data. No story, stats, gallery, location block or « Nous trouver » nav link appears without the fields that fill it, and nothing is ever filled with sample text.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** scope admin styling under `[data-admin]` and use the `--admin-*` variables, not literal hex values in new components.",
      "**Do** reuse the shared primitives in `components/admin/ui.tsx` (`Card`, `PageHeader`, `SettingsSection`, `Field`, `PrimaryButton`, `GhostButton`, `StatusBadge`, `Tabs`).",
      "**Do** keep a single primary action per page header.",
      "**Do** keep status and channel colours identical on every screen (list, detail, calendar spans).",
      "**Do** respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; admin motion is limited to the 0.22s `admin-fade-in` page entrance and 0.15s colour transitions.",
      "**Do** build a new public world as one stylesheet that fills the whole `--s-*` contract under `.site[data-tpl=\"…\"]`, plus a `WORLDS` entry with default host colours and a font pair loaded with `preload: false`.",
      "**Do** bound every host colour in OKLCH before text sits on it.",
      "**Do** hide a public block when the host has not filled it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use terracotta as a button fill or a large background.",
